        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on scope, key pain points, and confirm the quarter-end close workflow map.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, let's kick off the Quarter-End Financial Close Process Streamlining project. The main goal is to standardize our process to improve speed and accuracy. Our first step is T1: mapping all current close activities. To start, could everyone please share the top 1-2 pain points you face during the close?",
            "mentions": [
              5553,
              75794,
              326471,
              440036
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 326471,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for starting this. For me, the biggest issue is tracking down manual journal entry approvals at the last minute. It always creates a bottleneck on the final day.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 440036,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "For T1, should I schedule meetings with each of you to get the list of activities?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Let's try a more async approach first to save time. Can you create a shared spreadsheet where everyone can list their tasks, who they hand off to, and any dependencies? We can use last quarter's checklist as a starting point.",
            "mentions": [
              440036
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "ok_hand",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 5553,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I agree, the approvals are a problem. Also, finding the right supporting documents for old accruals takes a lot of time.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
