        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define exception handling, compliance checks, and sign-off responsibilities.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, for T5, I've drafted the Exception Handling and Late Adjustment Procedure, which you can find in A4. The goal is to have a clear, auditable process for when things don't go as planned. Please review and share your feedback.",
            "mentions": [
              5553,
              326471,
              440036,
              75794
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 326471,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Reading through it now. The criteria for what constitutes a 'high-impact' issue are clear. I like the proposed approval flow. For logging these exceptions, will we use a specific tool or just a shared spreadsheet?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "For now, a simple shared spreadsheet is sufficient, as long as it captures all the fields listed in A4. We can revisit if the volume becomes too high.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 5553,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "The document says the Accounting Manager needs to approve adjustments over a certain amount. What if they are on leave?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Good question. Section 3.2 of the guideline A4 specifies that the Head of Finance is the designated backup approver. This ensures we don't have a single point of failure.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 98074,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Any other questions on the approval flow for late adjustments? If everyone is comfortable with the process outlined in A4, we can confirm it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 326471,
